    '|b||Between 1610 and 1675, Trinity House, the official lighthouse authority, built none. Private individuals built at least ten.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8800
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:ujricf'
    '|a||And of the forty-six lighthouses standing in 1820, thirty-four had been built by private individuals.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1xrps3c'
    '|b||So how did they get paid, if the beam can''t be switched off?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4160
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1gdoz5n'
    '|a||At the port, not at sea. The owner got a patent from the Crown, and ships paid a toll for each light they passed, collected by customs when they docked.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1qmr4nh'
    '|b||The beam can''t keep anyone out, but the harbour can. Tie the light to something excludable, and it can be sold.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7240
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:aa8u53'
    '|a||Coase''s verdict: economists should stop using the lighthouse as a service only the government could provide.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:13f48cp'
    '|b||But look at who made that work. The Crown granted the monopoly and fixed the toll, its customs officers collected it, and every ship paid, like it or not.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8880
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1h5nrnm'
    '|a||Critics such as Van Zandt and Bertrand call that a state-enforced tax, not a market. And in 1836 Parliament had Trinity House buy the private lights out.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:lgte47'
    '|b||So how sure are we? That free riding leaves public goods underprovided is mostly agreed. Whether Coase''s lights were really private is contested.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10360
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1ibep46'
    '|a||And today, British lighthouses still run on light dues, paid by ships calling at British and Irish ports.':
